  "name": "Summarize a YouTube video with AI",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Summarize a YouTube video with AI\n\n**Who's it for**\nAnyone who wants the gist of a YouTube video without watching it - researchers, content marketers, students, or AI agents that need to reason over video content.\n\n**What it does**\nTakes a YouTube video URL, fetches the full spoken transcript via the GetYouTubeTranscript API, then sends that transcript to an AI model to produce a short summary.\n\n**How it works**\n1. Set your video URL in the \"Video URL to Summarize\" node.\n2. The GetYouTubeTranscript node fetches the transcript (1 credit per call, free tier available - no card required).\n3. An HTTP Request node sends the transcript to OpenAI's Chat Completions API to summarize it.\n4. The final Set node formats the video title + summary as clean output.\n\n**Requirements**\n- A free GetYouTubeTranscript API key: https://getyoutubetranscript.com (100 free credits, no card required)\n- An OpenAI API key (or swap the HTTP Request node for any other LLM provider)\n\n**How to customize**\n- Change the prompt in the HTTP Request node's body to ask for bullet points, a tweet-length summary, key quotes, etc.\n- Swap the Manual Trigger for a Form Trigger to let others submit URLs themselves.\n- Chain additional nodes (Slack, Notion, Google Sheets) to save or share the summary automatically.\n\n**Note:** this uses the GetYouTubeTranscript community node, which requires a self-hosted n8n instance (community nodes aren't available on n8n Cloud). See the workflow screenshot in the template listing since community-node previews don't render inline.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 1900,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "326a842a-3fb5-4ded-bfc3-e802a19d3cb7",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Template Description",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
